Alex: opened a PR to consolidate fallback examples into a compact guidance page and swap long examples for SDK-first snippets. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/8420. Need sanity check on 429, timeouts, context-trim samples.
Priya: on it. Prioritize JS retry + graceful stream degrade then python context-trim helper?
Alex: yes—compressing 3 variants into one canonical pattern + short alternatives.
Matt: runtime note: don't recommend aggressive prefix cache TTL without a caveat; can cause stale interactive responses. Add a one-line warning. :warning: 
Priya: will add caveat. Also call out expected headers (Retry-After, X-RateLimit-Remaining) so SDKs can use them.
Sarah: infra: preferred transient signal is 429 with Retry-After in seconds. Sometimes 429 lacks Retry-After; clients should use exponential backoff + jitter when missing.
Kevin: updating JS snippet to use Retry-After if present, else exp backoff + jitter. Proposed snippet: ```js
async function callWithRetries(req, max=3){
  for(let i=0;i<max;i++){
    const res = await fetch('/v1/generate', req);
    if(res.status===429){
      const ra = res.headers.get('retry-after');
      if(ra) await wait(parseInt(ra)*1000);
      else await wait(Math.pow(2,i)*100 + jitter());
      continue;
    }
    return res;
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}
```
Priya: add a comment about not retrying non-idempotent requests unless server dedupe available.
Alex: added paragraph about idempotency and chat vs generate endpoints.
Julia: DocsBot: PR 8420 updated  added "Compact fallback patterns" and removed duplicate examples. CI: https://ci.redwood-inference/internal/8420/checks.
